  {
   "id": 13,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    40,
    560
   ],
   "size": [
    420,
    320
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "## pixel-art-restyle.json\n\nExisting image -> pixel art, REDRAWN (img2img with the pixel-art LoRA)\n\n**Does:** re-paints the source with `pixel-art-xl` before making a sprite, so detail is simplified into the pixel idiom instead of being resampled. `KSampler` is img2img at the model's native resolution: `denoise` **0.6** is the knob - low keeps the source, high redraws it (0.8 moves noticeably further). Then `PixelArtDetectorConverter` at a **fixed 64x64** with a chosen palette makes the grid (`paletteList` from `PixelArtLoadPalettes`; pico-8 by default). Two saves: the redrawn image at full size and the 64 px sprite.\n**Do NOT downscale before the sampler.** A 64-128 px latent makes SDXL produce mush - measured: a 128 px latent at denoise 0.93 returned a colour blob, not a knight. Downscaling belongs at the END, with the known factor.\n**Faithful instead?** `pixel-art-convert.json` keeps the source exactly (resize + palette, no redraw). **Restoring an existing small sprite?** that is a third job - upscale it first so the model can work at native resolution (the `comfyui-pixelart-detector` pack ships an example for it), which is not what this flow does.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S10** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E5** nodes + **E31/E32** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "properties": {},
   "order": 0
  }
